{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1513","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1513","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1513\",\"parent_revision\":\"2333508499f5638ad75ac5248c569359f144c18ffbe75a7bcf76beebd54f6ba9\",\"root_revision\":\"2333508499f5638ad75ac5248c569359f144c18ffbe75a7bcf76beebd54f6ba9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAfter P912, local_yaml.py is 507 code LOC and server.py is 527 code LOC \u2014 both above the 500 LOC threshold flagged by code review. File size at this scale makes navigation and isolated testing harder. The code review identified these as candidates for decomposition into smaller focused modules.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nVERIFIED (LOC counts understated) \u2014 Both files exceed 500 total lines and the violation is larger than described.\\n\\nEvidence (`wc -l` on current HEAD):\\n- `local_yaml.py`: **656 total lines** (issue states 507 \u2014 delta is 149 lines; prior count was likely code-only LOC excluding blanks/comments)\\n- `server.py`: **621 total lines** (issue states 527 \u2014 same explanation)\\n\\nBoth files substantially exceed the 500-line threshold. The code review figures appear to be non-blank, non-comment line counts; total file length is 31\u201336% higher than stated.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: refactor\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` \u2014 656 lines, primary decomposition target\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 621 lines, primary decomposition target\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/` \u2014 destination directory for local_yaml submodules\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/` \u2014 destination directory for server submodules\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nLarge files increase cognitive load during navigation and make isolated unit testing harder. Each file currently mixes multiple responsibilities. `local_yaml.py` blends plan CRUD, task CRUD, document operations, and address resolution. `server.py` blends MCP tool definitions, request routing, helper functions, and backend lifecycle. Severity: low (no functional defect), but compounding: each new feature added to these files makes the problem worse.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #1492 (docstring fix) should land first \u2014 avoids refactoring code that is concurrently being corrected\\n- #1514 (create_plan exception fix) should land first \u2014 same reason\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### local_yaml.py decomposition\\n- [ ] Plan CRUD operations extracted to a focused module (e.g., `backends/local_yaml_plans.py`)\\n- [ ] Task CRUD operations extracted to a focused module (e.g., `backends/local_yaml_tasks.py`)\\n- [ ] Document operations extracted to a focused module (e.g., `backends/local_yaml_documents.py`)\\n- [ ] `LocalYamlTaskProvider` class in `local_yaml.py` delegates to extracted modules; file drops below 300 lines\\n- [ ] All existing tests pass without modification after decomposition\\n\\n### server.py decomposition\\n- [ ] MCP tool handler functions grouped by domain into submodules (e.g., `server_plan_tools.py`, `server_task_tools.py`)\\n- [ ] Helper functions (`_validated_task_patch`, `_get_backend`, etc.) moved to a `server_helpers.py` or equivalent\\n- [ ] `server.py` retains only MCP app initialization and tool registration; file drops below 200 lines\\n- [ ] All existing MCP tool signatures remain identical (no breaking changes to callers)\\n- [ ] All existing tests pass without modification after decomposition\\n\\n### Shared\\n- [ ] No circular imports introduced\\n- [ ] Public API surface (imports from `sam_schema`) unchanged\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files <changed files>` passes with zero lint/type errors\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: M\\nReasoning: Two files, purely structural decomposition with no behavior change. Risk is import graph correctness and ensuring no public API breaks. Estimated 3\u20135 hours including test validation pass.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **local_yaml.py and server.py exceed 500 loc threshold \u2014 need decomposition** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: QG T1 code review of P912 \u2014 follow-up plan P1429\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"af4c68ffad34e485a6b4fe952d12aa18051a16909357b514bcc6b6b56be10707\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdr0jQ\"}"}